 "text": "Hello, how are things with you? That's usually the room you' in, not the microphone. Try in a quiet corner far from windows. Then move to the kitchen. Stand away from anything metal, like the fridge. Then put blankets and pillows around the mic to dampen reflections. A cheap carpet or a thick blanket on the wall gives big improvement. A few inches are enough, but the closer you get, the more you dampen your own sound. Good experiment. In the meantime, open your window a crack when raining, or turn on fan if it' windy.",
